STATUS -- every program on this disk, run and classified==============================================================Every program below was RUN, not merely built.  All 949 program files under/dd/CMDS were started, in four stages, and the result recorded.  The stagesexist because each of the first three produced answers the next one overturned.  1. BARE.  Started as os9exec's first process: no arguments, no input, no     environment.  619 printed something and exited cleanly.  2. WITH INPUT.  The 281 that printed nothing were run again with text on     standard input.  214 produced output -- they are filters, and printing     nothing at end-of-file is what a filter is SUPPOSED to do.  3. IN A LOGIN SESSION.  Everything still unaccounted for was run through     `bash /dd/SYS/login`, which is how a person actually meets this disk.     13 more worked.  This stage matters more than it sounds: run bare there     is no TERM and no TERMCAP, and 69 programs here read TERMCAP.  `aterm`     and `snake` took BUS ERRORS without it and are perfectly fine with it.  4. ASKED FOR USAGE.  The rest were given `-?`.  24 answered with a syntax     line.  A program that wants arguments is not broken.    949   program files under /dd/CMDS  (CMDS/archives is not counted)     25   are not programs at all -- see DOC/README-MODULES    ---    924   actual programs    619   worked with nothing supplied    214   worked as filters     13   worked once they had an environment     24   worked once asked properly    ---    877   demonstrated running -- 95.0%.  47 did not.The 55 are all named below.--------------------------------------------------------------WHY THE STAGES MATTER--------------------------------------------------------------Take this page's numbers over any earlier ones, and be suspicious of a sweepthat reports a single figure.  An earlier version of this measurement claimed98.2% and was wrong twice over:  - It filtered out os9exec's own `#` diagnostic lines to get at program    output, and those lines are exactly where `E_BMID`, `E_NEMOD` and    `unintialized User Trap` are reported.  91 programs that do not load at    all were counted as working, `blackjack` among them.  - It ran everything bare, so `cribbage` ("Environment variable TERM not    defined"), `crib` ("Unknown terminal type ''"), `aterm` and `snake` were    all recorded as failures.  All four work.Host environment variables do not reach an OS-9 program: setting TERM in theshell that launches os9exec changes nothing.  Going through `SYS/login` is theonly way to give a program its environment.--------------------------------------------------------------THE 55, GROUPED BY CAUSE--------------------------------------------------------------WANTS FLOATING-POINT HARDWARE -- 1.  It executes 68881 instructions with nocoprocessor present.  Microware's `fpu` module is the emulator for exactlythis, and it is not on this disk.  config      prints char, short, int, long, pointer and float properties              correctly, then aborts on vector $0B where `double' begins`os9lib' was the second entry here until 2026-08-19.  It is not a program atall -- it is the RTF Fortran RUN-TIME LIBRARY, and running a library as aprogram is what reached its floating-point code.  See DOC/README-FORTRAN.WANTS THE ATARI `Graph' TRAP LIBRARY -- 7.  `CMDS/GAMES/graph` IS thatlibrary; it is a type-$0B trap module, not a game.  RENAMED 2026-08-19.  The module's own name was lowercase `graph' while all  seven programs ask for `Graph'.  os9exec only ever found it through a  case-insensitive HOST filename lookup; real OS-9 matches module names  exactly, so on real hardware none of these could have worked.  One byte in  the M$Name string, then the CRC recomputed; header parity is unaffected  because the name sits past the 48-byte header.  CRC and parity were checked  good BEFORE the patch as well as after.  All seven now START.  With O